      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the exact value of $\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$.",
        "Rearrange the equation: $\\tan^{-1}(4x) = -\\frac{\\pi}{6} - \\frac{\\pi}{6} = -\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.",
        "Take the tangent of both sides: $4x = \\tan\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\sqrt{3}$, and solve for $x$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate the exact inverse cosine term on the right-hand side:\n$$\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\implies -\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) = -\\frac{\\pi}{6}$$",
        "Rearrange the equation to isolate $\\tan^{-1}(4x)$:\n$$\\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\tan^{-1}(4x) = -\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\implies \\tan^{-1}(4x) = -\\frac{\\pi}{6} - \\frac{\\pi}{6} = -\\frac{2\\pi}{6} = -\\frac{\\pi}{3}$$",
        "Apply the tangent function to both sides:\n$$4x = \\tan\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\sqrt{3}$$",
        "Solve for $x$ in exact surd form:\n$$x = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$$"
      ],
